# Lambdas — the syntax

## `(parameters) -> body`

```java
()      -> 42            // no params
x       -> x * 2         // one — parens optional
(x, y)  -> x + y         // several — parens required
```

Types are inferred (rarely written).

## Two body forms

```java
x -> x * 2               // expression — its value is the result
x -> { return x * 2; }   // block — explicit return
```

Prefer the expression form when it fits.

## Target typing

A lambda has **no type of its own** — it takes it from the functional interface in context:

```java
Runnable r           = () -> System.out.println("hi");   // → run()
Comparator<String> c = (a, b) -> a.length() - b.length(); // → compare()
```

Same shape, different target. → can't assign a lambda to bare `var`.

## Everyday
`forEach(x -> …)` · `removeIf(s -> s.isBlank())` · `sort((a,b) -> …)`
